 a latent danger, then the kindest thing you can do—for both of you—is not marry him. Not because he’s dangerous, but because he deserves to be married to someone who isn’t waiting for him to turn into a monster. And you deserve a marriage where you can rest in the person you chose, not keep one eye on the emergency exit. This is not about ignoring things to avoid sounding prejudiced. It’s about doing the real, hard work of knowing the man you’re marrying, trusting the evidence of your own eyes, and then making a decision based on him—not on the ghosts that others have handed you.
